#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522e13cc-675f-57a2-bbc5-ed75ae553870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369931} {:answer/id #uuid "35ba7284-4f01-5b00-a8ca-edfa5ef970dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369932} {:answer/id #uuid "040a72bc-fcc4-5951-9b21-1f567cd49fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369933} {:answer/id #uuid "bea95ccd-eb23-5943-81d1-6cd549174be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{21}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369934} {:answer/id #uuid "862a7138-26dc-55f5-80f6-f8b12c4f81fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bea95ccd-eb23-5943-81d1-6cd549174be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{21}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369934} :answer-field/id #uuid "62a718ae-f4a8-5f07-ba0a-54def0cf1028" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44f4b45a-a44b-58c2-a3d0-cbe2e2bd55b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163602" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and the line $y=x.$ Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=15My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 15My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}{x}^{2}y+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})-(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{6}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15M{[\\frac{3}{20}{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{14}{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{36}{x}^{9}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =15M(\\frac{3}{20}-\\frac{1}{14}-\\frac{1}{36}) \\\\  & =15M\\cdot \\frac{16}{315} \\\\  & =\\frac{16M}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16M}{21}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{\\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{21}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f9db5c-e164-5da8-8198-fa6bb66ab5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278599} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4abe59-3a00-5413-9a13-f76e53a05f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278827} {:answer/id #uuid "27295108-8d28-5e44-bd4c-fd9f5f5c1dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278939} {:answer/id #uuid "2a222fa5-d9c5-5841-9ffa-a9c00a82be6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278965} {:answer/id #uuid "9a04f08e-efba-5b0c-ad94-d016db6f7419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a4abe59-3a00-5413-9a13-f76e53a05f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278827} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1724ad2-5623-51fe-a835-78c2ea54e619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd3dc29c-e508-5e62-812f-85ffd3f21aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-163609" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=3x,$ $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{5}+9{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}[2{x}^{6}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}\\cdot (128-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d303cc35-cf47-55c6-806e-3da1fff40c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369938} {:answer/id #uuid "cc834ea5-1c5b-546b-be71-3eb7b86763f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369939} {:answer/id #uuid "df1bf9ed-dda8-506e-96e7-3f7193831d72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369940} {:answer/id #uuid "06891c90-e7ba-5a49-8b01-b25f5dff77ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369941} {:answer/id #uuid "3dfb815d-eb8c-59f4-b6fe-9d5669446427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d303cc35-cf47-55c6-806e-3da1fff40c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369938} :answer-field/id #uuid "389c7304-cde4-5e40-a301-1d68ccd3a542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd312e64-46c6-5ed4-b65d-22fbf05ffa3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163611" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{3},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=5Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{x}^{2}\\cdot 5Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{[\\frac{1}{7}{x}^{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =5M\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03680dad-3bcf-5b29-abba-9ff2a1e3d2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278612} {:answer/id #uuid "5e763cc2-b9bb-5930-8d85-81b17df9e5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279458} {:answer/id #uuid "7915aba8-9f3f-5ecd-a4e8-b8564ca12b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279672} {:answer/id #uuid "a75d52ce-0daf-59d4-ab59-5619ccbc76f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{20}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280074} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f7c1a9-3d3e-52db-86b1-4f9a0a3192a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4f7c1a9-3d3e-52db-86b1-4f9a0a3192a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6fe166b-63e4-522d-a911-75e796a5f2ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41aab4a9-697e-5db4-a3bf-1e7d24bbc956" :question/math-academy-id "q-163613" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{6}x{y}^{6}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{20}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198419 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b3b03b-db7c-5e14-bf30-0c8e621a1cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282153} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6feef2-1cdf-5a8f-af31-d193a5e7b5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282344} {:answer/id #uuid "9b583607-518c-5a2b-857a-27893d2e3e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283043} {:answer/id #uuid "ee827f89-c824-5a29-84e7-d603d75dd34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283769} {:answer/id #uuid "f2efdc3d-8ffc-5626-8aeb-007c3da3965a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c6feef2-1cdf-5a8f-af31-d193a5e7b5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282344} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ff9427d-b4f4-5845-9d75-84d60b4d221a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e21ba823-c822-5cad-82d7-ecb3f63bc4fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-163657" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region between two circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{x}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{1}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{21}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
